ng to keep coming throughout the  entire process as more and more updates  happen about your vehicle so you don't  actually need to keep checking your  Tesla account because you're either  going to get a text message or an email  or both with an update of what's going  on they will then redirect you to this  Tesla account so make sure you set up  your account go through all the details  fill in the background information and  make make sure your Tesla account is 100  set up ready to go if you're like me and  in most cases you're going to order your  Tesla and nothing's going to happen for  a little while for example we ordered  the Tesla Model y day one in Australia  we ordered it in the afternoon so we're  unfortunately pushed back to the second  shipment that means we waited five  months for our vehicle I know this isn't  a very long time especially some people  waiting years however you are most  likely going to be waiting a little  while it isn't going to be an instant  delivery the time period between  notifications is most likely going to be  quite long but what you can do is  actually try and figure out your vehicle  VIN number well and truly before you  have any paperwork so there is a free  VIN application that you can download  and install into Google Chrome it's  simply called Tesla Vin finder I'll link  it down below to make it easy for you  guys absolutely no affiliation I just  used it to try and figure out what my  VIN was extremely early if you don't  want to download and install the VIN  finder you can search through the source  code of the actual account page to  figure out if your VIN is available on  not this is just a bit more of a tedious  task about two months before we took  delivery of our brand new model y we got  a text message from Tesla saying your  documentation for registration is now  ready what you have to do is jump online  onto your account fill out this  paperwork and then email it through  Tesla they don't tell you about this  nobody tells you where to send it you  actually have to do a little bit of  research to figure out where it needs to  go so out of pure excitement I managed  to fill out all these paperwork  immediately send it back to Tesla and  again no news is supposedly good news  unfortunately for me I ended up having  to resend this email about three or four  times and even still there was a mad  rush the day before we took our delivery  to actually get this paperwork finished  so I do strongly recommend that whenever  you send these paperwork across the  Tesla give them a quick call or a quick  follow-up email just to make sure that  they have received this documentation I  know they don't want you to contact them  I know they want to be left alone but  unfortunately in my situation it was  almost delayed delivery just because  they had so many emails come through and  they completely mislined if you've  already downloaded the Tesla app when  you actually purchased your vehicle  you're going to see the estimated  delivery date or the EDD change at this  point in time as well for me personally  it jumped to a two-week window at the  very start of November some people have  told me that their edds haven't actually  changed until the vehicle has arrived in  the country so sometimes your very large  window of three months we'll drop down  to two weeks quite early other times  you're going to have to wait a little  bit longer don't get too excited though  that first two week estimated delivery  date is just basically a lie most of the  time you're not going to get it in that  first two week block that two weeks is  going to continuously jump around so  don't plan things around that two-week  delivery time actually wait until you  have something locked in before you  start finalizing bits and pieces now  about six weeks before we took delivery  we got another text message from Tesla  saying your final invoice is ready we  mistakenly actually took this as a great  sign that our model y was in the country  and unfortunately that wasn't the case  but we did end up paying the invoice off  at that point in time what you need to  know is you do not have to pay for this  model y or any of the Teslas until 48  hours before delivery usually I'd  recommend three to four days before that  just so you can make sure that all the  bank transfers go through properly  especially if you're going through  Finance if you do want to pay an  installments and pay this vehicle off  whilst you're waiting you can actually  contribute to this bank account that  they provide you with and slowly start  paying off in installments once the  final invoice is activated you will just  get a numerous amount of emails and text  messages afterwards saying your final  balance has been updated that means  they've received your money and you can  just keep topping it off as you go along  they will keep track of it so it is okay  if you do wish to actually pay off  installments and not just do one big  lump sum if you didn't install that then  find a back in the day then you can also  find your VIN right now on this final  invoice this bin is going to allow you  to figure out where your vehicle is how  it's tracking and where it's being  shipped to about seven days after you  receive your final invoice is available  message you're going to get another one  from Tesla now Tesla's going to give you  an update saying that your model y has  been assigned to your order this is  again great news it means that delivery  date is inching closer now at this point  in time once you have your VIN number  and once you have your vehicle assigned  to you you can actually go ahead and  start tracking it there are two ways to  do this you can do this 100 free or you  can actually go through a paid service I  think the paid service is probably very  good and probably worth the money  considering how much time I dedicated to  trying to track down my vehicle so if  you want to pay the money I believe the  account is better Prime you can find it  through Google it's quite easy to find  and utilize their service instead what I  managed to figure out is that my vehicle  was on a row row ship all Teslas go on  row row ships and through these railroad  ships you can then determine which  carrier it is and where they're actually  being shipped from in Australia there  are only two row row carriers that come  in at the moment it's actually only one  taking up predominantly most of the  delivery that company is mole Ace  m-o-l-a-c-e once you have your VIN  number you can jump onto the mole Ace  website go to the search function change  over to a VIN number paste in your  actual VIN number and it will tell you  which vessel your car is on once you've  figured out what vessel it's on then you  can simply type in that vessel name into  Google directly and jump onto vessel  finder in my instance for example it was  on a ship called Victorious Ace that  means I went on Google typed in  Victorious Ace and it quickly told me  exactly where that ship was I knew when  it was going to be arriving at the Port  I knew when it was going to be departing  its next destination now this  information could be either good or bad  for you because you could be like me and  way too invested as soon as I knew that  boat was coming in I was checking the  vessel finder all the time I was  tracking it as it was moving through the  ocean and I was waiting for it to hit  the port once it hit the Fremantle Port  I jumped on the Harbor cams I was  watching that vehicle come in and unload  and then I was still tracking as those  Teslas were being trucked out to the  delivery Center so for me it was bad  because I was so emotionally invested  into this situation that I thought the  delivery was coming very soon  unfortunately what happened like most  people say is my estimated delivery date  actually changed as all of these  vehicles were shipped off the port  because our delivery Center has a very  small maximum capacity it meant they  were delivering them in batches and  unfortunately my car was somewhere at  the end of the batch so my delivery date  got pushed from the start of November to  the end of November even though the  vehicle was pushed back I knew that it  was now in the country and it classified  as a registered vehicle in Australia  you're able to jump onto a website  called the register of approved vehicle  search or ravs for short you can type in  your VIN number and it will  automatically tell you that this vehicle  has or hasn't been registered in  Australia usually once they come off the  port and they've been cleared through  customs then they also get entered into  rabs this rabs is one of the most final  crucial steps because that means your  estimated delivery date is coming very  very soon for me personally once those  delivery dates started jumping around it  only took one business day before I got  another text message from Tesla saying  your Tesla Model Y is now ready for  scheduled delivery the schedule delivery  text message was great all you had to do  was literally jump on your phone press  the link sent to you in the text message  and then pick a day that was convenient  for you unfortunately for us here in  Western Australia the delivery Center is  only open throughout the week and the  delivery time slots weren't very good  for instance we picked it up on a Friday  at 9 30 in the morning that was the only  time slot available that week you cannot  pick it up over the weekend you can only  pick it up at these specified times so  if your workplace or your lifestyle  isn't flexible you might actually have  to think around how you can go and pick  up this vehicle like I mentioned  previously there was a mad rush to get  our paperwork and documentation sorted  the day before delivery actually  occurred however the day before delivery  for us and in our situation we go to  Tesla express delivery confirmation now  I would believe believe that you would  get this text message significantly  sooner if they'd sorted out your  paperwork when they were supposed to but  for us it literally was the day before  nonetheless this was a good text message  to receive because it means your vehicle  is ready for delivery it's scheduled and  waiting for you now delivery Day Has  Come and it is one of the most exciting  days it is unlike any other luxury car  experience now when you usually buy a  luxury car you walk into the dealership  there's all sorts of shows there's some  champagne there's probably flowers and  they peel off the magical rug over the  car with Tesla however you walk into an  old Warehouse you approach a bench full  of Tesla staff you show them your app  and you show them your driver's license  you have to accept delivery before you  even see the car they walk you to your  vehicle and walk away so they are truly  expecting you to know everything about  this vehicle before you even take  delivery they want you to know how to  use the app they want you know how to  use the screen they're not really too  keen on showing you unless they  genuinely have to so make sure you do  your research and keep looking at all  these Tesla videos they are incredible  be helpful and there are some great  content creators on YouTube to be able  to explain all of this our vehicle in  Australia obviously came from the  Shanghai Factory and it was 99.99  perfect there was genuinely no Faults  that we could see with it on the day  there was no panel gaps there was no  scratches it was Immaculate there was a  little bit of dust here and there but  that's not really something you can be  too upset about and we didn't really  have to go through that full checklist  because once you go through that  checklist I feel like it removes the  enjoyment and excitement about your  delivery experience you have to go  through meticulously tick off all these  items and figure out if anything is  wrong with your brand new purchase  thankfully the production is getting  significantly better and the Shanghai  Factory is producing vehicles that are  nearly Flawless like I said 99.99 there  still was a 0.1 error in our vehicle  unfortunately the seat belts for some  reason on the rear white seats left  small little scuff marks we can't get  them out with email Tesla so we'll see  what happens with that situation but  unfortunately I think there's some sort  of Grease or oil on those seat belts and  as they rest and sit on those white  seats they eventually leave marks be  prepared that your model y will most  likely not come with 100 fully charged  ours came with a 93 charged which was  still really really good once we charged  it to 100 it indicated to us that we  could drive 435 kilometers on a single  charge now we live about 500 kilometers  away from this delivery Center so we put  that to the test literally on the first  day unfortunately you're nowhere near  that 400 kilometer range driving at 110  kilometers an hour basically in pristine  perfect conditions it only managed to  hit about 300 kilometers before it was  indicating it needs to stop at a  Supercharger so luckily for us there is  one supercharger between us and that  manages to make the distance quite  easily it supercharges super quick in  about 20 minutes we went from 30 to 100  to make it back to our destination so  overall it was a good experience but  that is definitely one of the most  disappointing elements of the entire  order process is the fact that the range  is not as good as promised now I  understand that this was going to occur  but I just genuinely didn't think it was  going to be that much of a difference  compared to its estimator range to its  actual range anyway that's all for me  today guys thank you so much for  watching I hope this video gave you  clarity about your Tesla Model y  experience and what you can Expect When  You're Expecting I'm not sure if I'm  going to keep creating these Tesla  videos so feel free to leave a comment  down below if you want to see more of  these content potentially in some shorts  long form I'm not entirely sure but let  me know either way if you enjoyed the  content nonetheless feel free to hit  that subscribe button and like always  you will see me here next Monday

